        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. WHO declares global health emergency over Ebola outbreak in DR Congo Africa Issued on: 17/05/2026 - 11:23 General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus declared the Ebola disease outbreak in Congo and neighboring Uganda a public health emergency of international concern on Sunday after more than 300 suspected cases and 88 deaths. In a post on X, the World Health Organization said the outbreak does not meet the criteria of a pandemic emergency like the COVID-19 pandemic, and advised against the closure of international borders. Joint US-Nigeria operation killed a senior militant leader of IS 17/05/2026 Africa US and Nigeria claim killing of Islamic State second-in-command 16/05/2026 Africa Trump says Islamic State group leader was killed in a joint US-Nigerian mission 16/05/2026 Africa Congolese report constant burials as deaths in new Ebola outbreak reach 80 16/05/2026 Africa The dark side of Nigeria's crypto craze: Hope, scam and money laundering 14/05/2026 On the ground Africa From poachers to refuge: The world's only bonobo orphanage is hidden in DR Congo 14/05/2026 Africa How Sudanese children are going back to school in a refugee camp after years of war 14/05/2026 Africa Cape Verde: One of the driest countries on Earth heads to the polls 14/05/2026 Africa M23 rebels withdraw from several positions under US diplomatic pressure 14/05/2026 Africa"
